<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar output reaches 2.27 million tonnes.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar output reaches 2.27 million tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's sugar output as of January 30 was recorded at 2.27 million tonnes with the yield lower than the corresponding period last year, sources from the industry ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>They noted that although more sugar cane was crushed compared to the same period last year, the sugar output was less due to the weaker yield.</p>
<p>A total of 23.5 million tonnes of sugar cane were crushed by 46 mills across the country as of January 30 against 23.06 million tonnes last year during which 2.31 million tonnes of sugar were produced, they said.</p>
<p>Molasses production amounted to 927,415.3 tonnes with the yield of 39.34 kg per tonne of sugar cane.</p>
<p>The following is the comparison of this season's sugar cane crushing details with the same period last season (in tonnes unless otherwise specified):</p>
<p>					Jan 30 1997     Jan 30, 1996</p>
<p>Crushed sugar cane		 23,573,034	 23,068,068</p>
<p>Raw sugar			     1,398,336	  1,390,102</p>
<p>White sugar			     581,523	    598,600</p>
<p>Refined sugar			   294,468	    323,284</p>
<p>Yield (kg per tonne)		    96.48	     100.22</p>
<p>Commercial Cane Sugar (pct)	   11.07		11.69</p>
<p>Molasses				  927,415	    977,867</p>
<p>Yield					 39.34		42.39</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642 reuter ak dsc</p>
